          Does Converting JPG to PNG Improve Image Quality?
        </h2>
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            A common misconception is that converting a file format can magically enhance visual sharpness or clarity. <strong>Converting JPG to PNG does not reconstruct image data that was already discarded by lossy JPEG compression.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            When a JPEG is created, high-frequency chromatic variations and subtle color subtleties are permanently removed to minimize file weight. While converting the file to PNG encapsulates the picture in a lossless format that halts any further degradation during editing, it cannot restore detail that no longer exists in the source file.
          </p>
