          <p class="text-sm text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 leading-relaxed">
            Because JPG files possess no alpha transparency channel, converting a JPG to PNG will <strong>not automatically make its background transparent</strong>. The solid background color (such as white or gray) present in the original JPG will remain as solid pixels in the PNG output. To make a background transparent, you can open the newly created PNG in a graphic editing tool and remove the background color, which PNG now supports.
          </p>
        </div>
